- holeModel_verified_iff: closed typing, no hypotheses and zero cost specialize existing judge; arbitrary recorded status is ignored. Both positive and negative guards/supports/blockers are inhabited.
- holeDecision_verified_iff: arbitrary Boolean/Nat observations; true iff all four required observations hold.
- holeDecision_label: all seven membership disjuncts checked individually; none uniformly provable.
- holeAdmission_judge_iff: actual gate iff model judge, provided probe/current-world correspondence; the premise does not assert admission, but applicability to a deployed request must be proved separately.
- hole_judgment_admission_bridge: combines actual holeJudge and gate with independent clause/probe evaluations; no syntactic vacuity. The blocker observation premise hb is precisely what an omitted blocker may violate. Pending runtime counterexample, this is insufficient evidence of the advertised deployed model correspondence.
- hole_select_iff: actual Closure.select iff current judge under independent found-hole/candidate, chooser and unaccepted conditions; witnesses are returned closures, not arbitrary inhabitants.
- hole_fill_iff: actual Closure.fill (propose then select) recomputes judgment; historical status cannot decide success.
- hole_rejudge_status: actual indexed candidate updated to exact judgment, with no unchanged-state disjunct. Covers negative statuses, consistent with ROOT's rejudge ruling.
